        "narrationScript": "Alright team, let’s dive into our roleplay exercise centered around pitching Maestro to a Chief Revenue Officer who’s currently using Google Optimize, which, as we know, is reaching its end of life. They’re only running about 3-4 tests per month, so it’s our job to show them how a mature experimentation program can truly transform their decision-making.\n\nThe key here is to frame experimentation not just as a tool replacement, but as an essential infrastructure for enterprise-level decision-making. We want to help them see that implementing Maestro means more than just switching platforms; it’s about elevating their entire approach to experimentation.\n\nThroughout this roleplay, focus on two critical areas. First, emphasize the importance of testing governance. This ensures that experiments are not only well-managed but also aligned with their strategic goals. Next, outline a clear 90-day experiment backlog. This gives them a tangible roadmap to follow and highlights how quickly they can start seeing impactful results.\n\nRemember, our goal is to shift their mindset from seeing experimentation as an occasional test to recognizing it as a vital, ongoing process that drives growth and innovation.\n\nAs you practice, keep that transformation narrative front and center. Let’s get ready to show them how Maestro can be the game-changer they need! Now, let’s transition into discussing how to effectively manage objections in this scenario.",
