        "narrationScript": "Every e-commerce team has search problems — they just may not realize it yet. Today, let’s dive into four common pain categories that you can explore during your discovery conversations.\n\nFirst up, we have ZERO RESULTS. Picture this: \"20% of our searches return nothing.\" When that happens, customers leave, and that’s revenue lost. It’s crucial to implement AI fallback strategies to tackle this issue.\n\nNext, let’s talk about POOR RELEVANCE. Imagine a customer searching for \"gift ideas\" and being bombarded with 10,000 unrelated products. Without context or curation, the shopping experience falls flat.\n\nThen we have LOW CONVERSION. This is where people are searching and browsing but not buying. It’s likely that the search results aren’t optimized for purchase intent, making it difficult for customers to find what they truly want.\n\nFinally, there’s POOR DISCOVERABILITY. When customers can’t find your new products or seasonal collections due to manual merchandising delays, you’re missing out on significant sales opportunities.\n\nAs you engage with your prospects, ask them: \"What percentage of your site revenue comes from search? And what's the conversion rate on those searches?\" Remember, best-in-class search converts at 6-8%, while many brands are still stuck at 2-3%. \n\nIdentifying these pain points is your gateway to helping them improve and grow. Now, let’s transition into how we can position our solutions effectively to address these challenges.",
