        "imageUrl": "/uploads/slides/slide-solution-modules-7-1771057590891.png",
        "imagePrompt": "Create a professional presentation slide with dark navy blue (#1A2B8C) background. Title in large white bold text: \"ROLEPLAY: DYNAMIC BUNDLES PITCH\". Show a tug-of-war visual: left side \"MERCHANDISING: Wants higher AOV\" pulling against right side \"FINANCE: No blanket discounting\". In the center, a magenta (#E84C8A) solution bridge labeled \"DYNAMIC BUNDLES — Smart pairings, protected margins.\" Below, a sample bundle mockup: Product A ($45) + Product B ($35) = Bundle ($72, save $8). Target metrics: \"AOV Target: +14%\", \"Margin Floor: 40%\", \"Segments: New vs Returning.\" Bottom: \"GOAL: Bundle hypothesis + segments + guardrails.\" Professional negotiation scenario slide. 16:9 aspect ratio.",
        "narrationScript": "Alright, team, let’s dive into an exciting roleplay scenario that really showcases the power of dynamic bundles. Picture this: you’re meeting with a Merchandising Director who’s eager to boost their Average Order Value, but there’s a catch—the CFO has put the brakes on any blanket discounting. This is where your expertise comes into play.\n\nYour goal is to position dynamic bundles as the smart alternative to those sweeping discounts. You want to highlight how these bundles can elevate AOV without eroding margins, creating a win-win situation for both merchandising and finance.\n\nAs you prepare for this roleplay, think about the key criteria you need to meet. Make sure you define your bundle hypothesis clearly and identify the target segments that would benefit most from these bundles. And don’t forget to set specific AOV targets along with guardrails to keep everything on track.\n\nThe critical skill we’re honing here is balancing the merchandising goals with the finance constraints in a way that resonates with your audience. This is your opportunity to shine by proving that you can navigate these challenges effectively.\n\nSo, as we jump into the roleplay, remember to engage with your partner, ask the right questions, and most importantly, show them the value of dynamic bundles. Let’s get started and see how you can make this pitch resonate!",
