        "narrationScript": "Alright team, let’s dive into our roleplay scenario focused on the financial services sector. Imagine you're sitting across from the Chief Information Security Officer at a regional bank. They express a common concern: \"We can't run experiments — our compliance team won't allow JavaScript injection.\" \n\nNow, this is where your skills come into play. Your goal is to navigate these compliance objections by emphasizing how our network-layer architecture aligns perfectly with their security requirements. Think about it: network-layer testing can address their fears while still allowing us to demonstrate value.\n\nAs you engage in the conversation, keep in mind the criteria for success. You want to pave the way for an approved pilot path, establish compliant data boundaries, and most importantly, align with their security stakeholders. This is where speaking their language becomes crucial. You should be ready to discuss terms like HIPAA, SOC 2, and PII, showcasing your understanding of their regulatory landscape.\n\nSo, as you practice this roleplay, focus on how you can reassure the CISO that our approach not only meets compliance but also enhances their security posture. Remember, it's about building trust and demonstrating that you’re a partner in their journey. \n\nLet’s take these insights into our next exercise and refine how we present our solutions under scrutiny.",
