        "imageUrl": "/uploads/slides/slide-vertical-selling-11-1771057875044.png",
        "imagePrompt": "Create a professional presentation slide with dark navy blue (#1A2B8C) background. Title in large white bold text: \"ROLEPLAY: VERTICAL CURVEBALL — MULTI-BRAND\". Show a complex organizational chart with 5 brand logos and 12 country flags, all connected by messy lines (chaos). Below, a magenta (#E84C8A) transformation arrow pointing to a clean, structured governance model: \"Phase 1: Pilot Brand → Phase 2: Region 1 → Phase 3: Global Rollout.\" Persona: \"Global Head of Digital — 5 brands, 12 countries, tool sprawl.\" Bottom: \"GOAL: Governance model + phased rollout + MAP.\" Professional enterprise complexity slide. 16:9 aspect ratio.",
        "narrationScript": "Alright team, let’s dive into an engaging roleplay scenario that will sharpen our skills in managing enterprise complexity. Imagine you’re in a meeting with the Global Head of Digital at a multi-brand, multi-region enterprise. This organization is not just large; it’s sprawling across five distinct brands in twelve different countries. Their challenge? Tool sprawl, competing teams, and inconsistent governance are making it tough for them to operate efficiently.\n\nYour mission here is to help them navigate this multi-brand complexity with a phased governance approach. Think about it: the goal is to create a governance model that can adapt across various regions and brands. You’ll need to develop a phased rollout plan that addresses each brand's unique needs while ensuring seamless collaboration.\n\nTo pass this exercise, you’ll need to deliver a solid governance model, outline a phased rollout by region and brand, and craft a Mutual Action Plan that keeps everyone aligned. Remember, the key skill at play here is enterprise complexity management—your ability to turn chaos into a structured, actionable plan.\n\nAs you prepare for this roleplay, focus on how you can guide your prospects through their challenges and bring clarity to their situation. This practice will not only enhance your skills but also build your confidence in tackling real-world scenarios. Let’s get started!",
